Z||000000||thecage||12-10-2001||09:04 PM||||Well here it goes. I had a problem with 4spd 86gt. It was hard to get the car in 3rd gear, but would go. I also had a tough time getting the car in first at a stop light. I found I could slip it in first if I pumped the clutch a few times. Reverse also gave me some problems. As a percentage 3rd gave me 70% greif, 1st 20% & R 10%. Reverse would grind when I have the problem getting it in. 1st to 2nd and 3rd to 4th never a problem. Now my big problem. I took it to a shop fairly reputable in fiero's to have it looked at to see if it was pedal, hydralics, cables etc. The verdict was it was none of the above all those are ok. They said it was forks in the tranny or syncro gear in the tranny. Now my big problem on my way home as I let up on the gas I hear this rattle noise from tranny. When in gear and gas applied no problem but as I let up on the gas boy do I hear loud rattle(grind?). Now they did not do anything except roadtest the car. What the f--k happened. I can say this though that I had no problem getting the car into gear. The car seems to slip into gear, even 3rd with no problem. Help someone. Any ideas? Anyone know of a reputable tranny place in the Toronto Area.||||reg||1
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||12-10-2001||09:42 PM||||-------JUST AN OBSERVATION, NOT A DIAGNOSIS-------<P>What might have been done was an adjustment to the shift cable in the shift bracket. Now that it has been adjusted, there is less tolerance on the synchros ( more than likely ALL synchros are worn out if just one is, but most commonly the 1st gear synchro )<P> The transmission may have to be rebuilt <P>On a side note, we do have a 4spd MX6 instock, I can rebuild it for you from the ground up and have it out to you to solve this problem.<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
